# SyncTeX inverse search: Ctrl+click in the PDF jumps to the source in VS Code.
#
# sandbox must be none. zathura's seccomp filter is inherited by every process
# it spawns, and it kills pivot_root, which Chromium needs at startup — so the
# editor command silently fails under the default "normal" sandbox.
set sandbox none
set synctex true
# The `code` CLI has a ~1s slow path when its stdout is not a TTY. Zathura, being
# a GUI app, spawns it without a controlling terminal, so every jump paid that 1s.
# `script` allocates a pseudo-terminal, which takes the fast path (~0.1s). The
# single-quoted inner command is one argv element to script's -c; zathura parses
# it with g_shell_parse_argv, so the quoting survives substitution.
set synctex-editor-command "script -qec 'code --reuse-window --goto %{input}:%{line}' /dev/null"
